## Attribution in End-User-Facing Applications

An "End-User-Facing Application" is a product or service, built with or
including the Software, that you make available to people other than your own
personnel through an interface those people use directly. A website, a web or
mobile application, a desktop application, a command-line tool, or any
comparable interface is an End-User-Facing Application.

If you make an End-User-Facing Application available, you must credit Hookfish
somewhere a user of that application can reasonably find it. A credit satisfies
this requirement if it:

1. identifies Hookfish by name, for example "Powered by Hookfish" or
   "Uses Hookfish";

2. links to https://github.com/hookfish/hookfish; and

3. appears somewhere a user can reach, such as an about page, a settings,
   credits or acknowledgements screen, an open-source or third-party licenses
   page, a colophon, a footer, or published documentation.

You do not have to display the credit on every screen, and no credit is
required for your internal use and access, for non-commercial education, or for
non-commercial research. We may waive this requirement in writing.

This requirement applies for as long as a version of the Software is licensed
to you under the Functional Source License above. It does not survive that
version's Grant of Future License: once a version becomes available under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, that grant applies on its own terms.

